%erg v1
Title: Fix vacuous already-archived test in test_archive.sh
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created

--- body ---
`tests/test_archive.sh` lines 156-162:

```sh
OUT4=$($ERG archive "$FIXTURES" 2>&1)
if echo "$OUT4" | grep -q "already exists"; then
    fail "default: already-archived ticket triggers collision (got: $OUT4)"
else
    pass "default: already-archived ticket not re-processed"
```

This passes vacuously: `erg archive` only scans the top-level directory, so
`7001-closed-unblocked.erg` (already in `closed/`) is never examined on the
second pass and never triggers the collision path. The test cannot distinguish
"correctly skipped because already archived" from "silently ignored because the
scanner doesn't look there."

The actual collision-handling path is tested at lines 165-178 (destination
already exists). The fix is to remove the vacuous re-run case and replace it
with a comment explaining why double-archiving is a no-op by design (scanner
scope), or to test the property directly: create a ticket, archive it, then
attempt to archive it by ID a second time and verify nothing changes.
